*__pycache__*

node_modules

*.env


# Agent trace recorder output. Full payloads: balances, positions and the
# user's own messages. Diagnostics, never committed.
traces/

# Local database dumps (make db-dump). Full copies of the live DB: credentials
# hashes, balances, chat history. Backups and hand-offs, never commits --
# `seeds/` is the reviewable, per-user thing that IS committed.
dumps/

# Test run output. Regenerated by every suite run, byte-different on every
# machine, and never read by anything -- the 100% gates live in pytest.ini and
# vitest.config.ts, not in these files. CLAUDE.md and README describe them as
# what a run PRODUCES, which is exactly what they still are.
#
# They were tracked until PR #38, where they produced 21 of the 23 merge
# conflicts on their own. Hand-merging a coverage XML is meaningless work: the
# only correct resolution was ever "re-run the suite", which regenerates them
# anyway. Untracked here by team decision; publish them as CI artifacts if the
# evidence is ever needed off a developer's machine.
#
# .coveragerc is NOT here: it is configuration, not output.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
junit.xml
htmlcov/
frontend/coverage/

# Vite build output. The backend image runs `npm run build` itself in its
# frontend-builder stage (backend/Dockerfile), so a committed dist/ is never
# the one that ships -- it is a 2 MB bundle that conflicts on every merge and
# is overwritten during the build regardless.
frontend/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
